/*
 * lib/autocad/SLCadRenderer.sleela
 * SLeeLa Standard Library Definition.
 * Definition: Defines the SLeeLa standard-library type SLCadRenderer used within the autocad library family.
 */
#sleela 1.3
// Unified SLeeLa standard-library front-end object.
// Family: autocad. The library facade that names the one-call entry point a
// front end (CLI or the JavaFX AutoCAD Studio) uses to evaluate a plan
// (descriptions, dimensions, plans, notes) into geometry and render an AutoCAD
// DXF drawing.
//
// This file is part of the package "discovery surface": the SLeeLa compiler's
// `run` compiles a single self-contained file, so the executable, all-classes-
// in-one-file build of the renderer lives in `lib/autocad/autocad.sleela`
// (which inlines SLCadModel, SLCadPlan, SLCadDxf, and this renderer with a
// `main`). This definition documents the facade's shape; SLeeLa performs the
// whole computation. No new VM opcode is required -- only arithmetic, struct
// ops, native math `sqrt`, and the existing String concatenation.
class SLCadRenderer {
  String title;         // drawing title
  String units;         // drawing units (e.g. "mm")

  void begin(String t, String u) { title = t; units = u; }
  String drawingTitle() { return title; }
  String drawingUnits() { return units; }
}
